{
  "note": "Invalid local copies: each case mutates a valid example (in memory) and must be refused with exactly this code; nothing is written (local-copy.md §4, §9). Cases with `path` (round 2, R02-02) set/delete a value at a dot path (relative to the first entry matching `entry` when given) and are re-hashed, so only the typed validation can refuse them. Byte-level cases (oversize, depth, UTF-8, HTML, dependency depth) and the type-confusion sweep are generated by contract-check.ts.",
